# Google Places API (New) — powers the reviews section.
#
# 1. Create a browser API key in Google Cloud with the Places API (New) enabled.
# 2. Restrict it by HTTP referrer to your domains. A browser key is visible in
#    the page source by design; the referrer restriction is what protects it.
# 3. Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the key.
#
# The place id is optional — without it the site looks the listing up by name
# and address on first load, then caches the result for twelve hours.

VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
VITE_GOOGLE_PLACE_ID=

# --- Online store (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Server-side only: no VITE_ prefix, so these never reach the browser.
# Leave them out and the site runs as the plain catalogue it always was.
#
# DATABASE_URL    mysql://user:password@host:3306/database
# DATABASE_SSL    1 for a hosted database that requires TLS (most do)
# DATABASE_CA     only if the host signs with its own certificate authority
#                 (Aiven does): base64 of its ca.pem  (base64 < ca.pem)
# JWT_SECRET      any random string of 32+ characters (openssl rand -hex 32)
# ADMIN_PHONE     the admin's sign-in number, 03xxxxxxxxx
# ADMIN_PASSWORD  8+ characters; only used by `npm run db:seed` to create
#                 the admin account the first time
DATABASE_URL=
DATABASE_SSL=
DATABASE_CA=
JWT_SECRET=
ADMIN_PHONE=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
